      "content": "The opposition will aggressively attack the **unrealistic cost and the potential for hyper-inflation,** arguing that the necessary tax burden would either collapse the economy or that the money would simply drive up the cost of living to the point where the benefit is always insufficient.\n\nThey will also heavily lean on the **\"moral hazard of unearned income,\"** asserting that providing a guaranteed check fundamentally erodes the work ethic, leading to widespread societal decline and a loss of personal drive.\n\nFor the most devastating attack, the opposition will argue that **\"poverty is not a condition to be supported, but a problem to be *solved through targeted intervention and strong market support*,\"** framing UBI as a simplistic, ideological band-aid that ignores the root causes of systemic inequality and lack of opportunity the opposition can better fix.",
